# Pairs with AtomicOnOwner. The saga starts with k2 already counted as
# prepared, so it decides with only k1's bucket in place and k1 surfaces the
# batch before the terminal backstops k2.
MODULE: AtomicOnOwnerFoldSagaStartSkipsEntry
TARGET: AtomicOnOwner
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: the saga records k2 as dispatched before dispatching it, so the batch commits torn
PERTURBS: SagaStart

--- FIND
    /\ sg' = "exec"
    /\ UNCHANGED <<rmap, published, row, pend, term, sealed, retired, mp, mk, src, dst, mdone, cancels, prepped, told, dec, opDone, young, ackOn>>
--- REPLACE
    /\ sg' = "exec"
\* MUTATION: k2 counted as dispatched.
    /\ prepped' = {k2}
    /\ UNCHANGED <<rmap, published, row, pend, term, sealed, retired, mp, mk, src, dst, mdone, cancels, told, dec, opDone, young, ackOn>>
--- END
